  if (isKnownNonNegative(Z, SQ.getWithInstruction(&I)) &&
      isKnownNonNegative(MinMax, SQ.getWithInstruction(&I))) {
    Pred = ICmpInst::getFlippedSignednessPredicate(Pred);
  } else
    return nullptr;
}
```

The problem is that when we have an unsigned predicate like `ICMP_UGE` and the min/max intrinsic is signed, we're trying to flip the predicate but not properly considering the case where this conversion might not be valid.

